  "First certificate",
  "From an empty control plane to a minted, inventoried certificate.",
  "Connect an issuer and enroll an agent",
  "The setup wizard provisions the signer-backed internal CA and brings your first agent online.",
  "Request the credential",
  "Pick a profile and name the credential — approval stays a separate step, so nobody self-issues.",
  "Approve it",
  "A second operator signs off in the approvals queue; issuance happens only after the gate.",
  "See it in inventory",
  "The issued certificate lands in the inventory and starts counting toward estate health.",
  "Migrate from an existing CA",
  "Find everything the old CA issued, pin your rules, and cut new issuance over deliberately.",
  "Point discovery at your estate",
  "Create a network source covering the hosts and ranges your old CA issued for.",
  "Queue the first scan",
  "Run the source — findings stream into the console as the scan walks your targets.",
  "Review what was found",
  "Triage discovered certificates straight from the findings table: claim, tag, or dismiss.",
  "Pin your issuance rules",
  "A profile locks algorithms, lifetimes, and usages before any new issuance cuts over.",
  "Cut new issuance to trstctl",
  "Request replacements against the profile; the approval gate keeps the cutover deliberate.",
  "Watch estate health",
  "Estate health tracks external versus issued sources as the migration drains the old CA.",
  "Respond to a compromise",
  "Scope the blast radius, replace before you revoke, and leave a sealed evidence trail.",
  "Scope the blast radius",
  "Select the compromised credential on the graph and analyze — the impact is painted on the map.",
  "Replace, then revoke",
  "The incident workflow provisions the replacement before the compromised credential is revoked.",
  "Verify revocation",
  "Confirm the credential shows revoked in inventory and CRL distribution has picked it up.",
  "Collect the evidence",
  "The audit trail and its signed export are the incident's evidence pack.",
