  "Mark as not done",
  "Automate fleet TLS",
  "Machines enroll and renew themselves over ACME with DNS-01 proof — no humans holding certificates.",
  "Inspect the ACME surface",
  "The Protocols page shows the ACME directory, tenant binding, profile gates, and live responder status.",
  "Delegate DNS-01 validation",
  "Point _acme-challenge at the validation zone by CNAME; DNS-01 provider configs and the preflight check live here.",
  "Point an ACME client at the directory",
  "Any ACME client works; certbot with DNS-01 covers wildcards and hosts with unreachable ports.",
  "Bind certificates to their endpoints",
  "One endpoint-binding call queues issue and deploy together; delivery receipts land under Renewal readiness.",
  "Kubernetes workload identity",
  "Short-lived certificates for workloads with attestation before trust — no static secrets in pods.",
  "Register the cluster's attester",
  "Add the cluster JWKS as an attester trust source on the Workloads page — attestation before trust.",
  "Enable the SPIFFE Workload API",
  "Protocols shows the trust-domain and socket requirements plus live responder status for SVID issuance.",
  "Register workloads as identities",
  "Each service account becomes a managed identity so its certificates are inventoried and owned.",
  "Pick your integration path",
  "cert-manager ClusterIssuer, native CertificateSigningRequests, or SPIRE upstream — the reference doc has the manifests.",
  "Verify SVIDs are rotating",
  "Workload certificates appear in the inventory and rotate on their own — nothing static to steal.",
  "Enroll devices",
  "Network and embedded devices enroll over EST, SCEP, or CMP and renew before expiry.",
  "Inspect the enrollment registers",
  "EST, SCEP, and CMP registers, gates, and live responder status all live on the Protocols page.",
  "Fetch the CA chain",
  "Devices bootstrap trust by fetching the CA chain from the EST well-known endpoint.",
  "Enroll with a CSR",
  "POST the device CSR to simpleenroll; re-enroll before expiry with the same flow.",
  "Gate constrained and MDM clients",
  "Tiny IoT clients use one-time bootstrap tokens; MDM phones are gated by SCEP challenge policies.",
  "Manage secrets",
  "An encrypted store with versioning, short-lived credentials, one-time shares, scanning, and cloud sync.",
  "Enable the secrets surface",
  "Secrets are fail-closed until the surface is enabled and a key-encryption key file exists.",
  "Work the native store",
  "Browse the tree, create, reveal-once, rotate, and delete — metadata is durable, values are not re-rendered.",
  "Issue short-lived credentials",
  "Dynamic leases, PKI-as-a-secret, and transit/KMIP operations live under the Engines tab.",
  "Share without residue",
  "One-time shares self-destruct on redemption; ephemeral API keys reveal once and expire on their own.",
  "Scan for committed secrets",
  "Repository and third-party scans report redacted findings only — file, line, and fingerprint, never the value.",
  "Sync to where workloads read",
  "Push stored secrets to cloud and CI targets; the browser only ever sends the name and remote key.",
  "SSH at scale",
  "Replace standing SSH keys with short-lived certificates from a central CA, with revocation via KRL.",
  "Discover standing SSH access",
  "An SSH discovery source finds authorized keys across the fleet — orphaned keys get flagged.",
  "Review the key findings",
  "Triage discovered keys in the findings table before any host trusts the new CA.",
  "Roll trust out to hosts",
  "The rollout records hosts, health checks, and the rollback plan as evidence; the SSH page tracks status.",
  "Issue attested user certs",
  "Short-lived user certificates are gated on attestation, with principals and source addresses pinned.",
  "Revoke before expiry",
  "Revocation lands in the KRL that hosts already fetch — no per-host key surgery.",
  "Retire standing keys",
  "Once cert-based access holds, retire the standing keys and keep the rollout ledger as proof.",
  "Onboard a team",
  "An isolated tenant slice with SSO, roles, default-deny policy, and a signed audit trail.",
  "Mint the tenant token",
  "A tenant-scoped token is the team's boundary: everything it touches stays inside the tenant.",
  "Wire browser SSO",
  "OIDC, SAML, or LDAP config maps signed-in users to the tenant; SCIM keeps membership synced.",
  "Add people and assign roles",
  "People and roles shows who can sign in. Exact SSO mappings, permissions, access keys, sessions, and offboarding stay one disclosure or focused dialog away.",
  "Turn on default-deny policy",
  "Policy gates with dual control decide what issues; the Policy page explains every decision.",
  "Prove it with the audit trail",
  "Query events in the console and export the signed evidence bundle for compliance.",
  "Crypto agility & PQC",
  "Inventory your algorithms, pin the rules, and migrate quantum-vulnerable credentials deliberately.",
  "Queue a CBOM scan",
  "The scan inventories algorithms across TLS endpoints and host configs; Posture shows the results.",
  "Read your crypto posture",
  "Posture grades PQC readiness and lists the quantum-vulnerable assets worth migrating first.",
  "Trace crypto assets on the graph",
  "Crypto-asset nodes show which workloads and credentials share a vulnerable key.",
  "Pin algorithms in a profile",
  "A profile restricts allowed key algorithms so nothing new is minted on the old curve.",
  "Migrate and rehearse rollback",
  "The EE migration orchestrator moves assets to ML-DSA targets and can roll a run back — rehearse it.",
  "Run in production",
  "A real certificate, live health, rehearsed recovery, exportable audit, and tuned backpressure.",
  "Serve over your own certificate",
  "Point the server at your certificate and key files before anything else depends on it.",
  "Watch readiness and metrics",
  "readyz checks db, nats, and signer; Prometheus scrapes /metrics — System health summarizes the runtime.",
  "Rehearse backup and restore",
  "Encrypted full backups only count once a restore has actually been rehearsed.",
  "Export audit evidence",
  "Query policy decisions in the console and export the signed bundle auditors can verify.",
  "Tune limits, federation, air-gap",
  "Backpressure, passive-region federation, and air-gap mode are environment-driven; posture discloses their state.",
  "Build on the API",
  "One OpenAPI contract, a CLI at full parity, idempotent mutations, and typed SDKs.",
  "Fetch the contract",
  "The OpenAPI 3.1 document is the source of truth; the API playground turns it into a safe guided request.",
  "Drive it from the CLI",
  "The CLI covers every API operation — point it at the server with two environment variables.",
  "Make mutations idempotent",
  "Send a stable Idempotency-Key with every create so retries never double-write.",
  "Query the credential graph",
  "The same graph the console draws is queryable — nodes, edges, blast radius, reachability.",
